DECL	{"args":[{"name":"a","sort":{"sort":"track"}},{"name":"b","sort":{"sort":"track"}}],"body":"tt","contract":"Road user a overtakes and passes road user b on b's right: a overtakes and passes b from the rear, as drv.interaction.overtake_pass states it with the same window and the same heading tolerance, and makes the passage with b on its left. b is on a's left where the lateral component of b's bearing in a's frame (rel.bearing) is positive; the two are side by side where their projections on a's heading share length (rel.longitudinal_overlap at or above zero). The act begins at the last observation of the window behind at which b was ahead of a with their headings aligned within same_dir_cos. The act is recognized at the observation at which drv.interaction.overtake_pass holds for a and b, where b is on a's left there and at every observation since the act began at which the two are side by side. The concept holds at that observation only, and not again until b has again been ahead of a and then comes to be behind it. Conduct before the window behind is not read: a pass that takes longer than the window is not recognized. It denotes the relative motion of the two road users and the side on which a passes only: it says nothing of the lanes or the pavement a uses, of whether b moves, or of why a passes. Not denoted: a pass with b on a's right at the recognition or at some observation at which the two are side by side, which is a pass on b's left; a drawing alongside b that does not clear b; b ahead of a only while their headings are not aligned. Where b's bearing or the overlap of the two bodies is unobserved at an observation the passage reads, it is unknown.","definition":null,"id":"drv.interaction.overtake_pass_on_right","kind":"formula","narrowings":[{"kind":"no_atom","span":"with their headings aligned within same_dir_cos","why":"The onset of the act (the last observation of the window behind at which b was ahead of a with their headings aligned), from which the side-by-side observations the recognition reads are counted, needs the alignment of a's and b's headings at past observations. No name the record claims denotes it: rel.bearing gives b's direction in a's frame, rel.longitudinal_overlap the shared length of the projections, and drv.interaction.overtake_pass holds only at the recognition and exposes neither its onset nor the alignment. rel.same_direction would denote it but is not claimed; counting from the last ahead or the last behind observation instead would be an approximation, not the contract."}],"params":[{"name":"window","unit":"second"},{"name":"same_dir_cos","unit":"ratio"}],"residues":[],"supersedes":null}
